From: Angelo Compagnucci <angelo.compagnucci@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] spi: atmel: allow changing bits_per_word between transfers

The controller advertises 8 to 16 bits per word, but the word size is
programmed in the chip select register only in setup(), and a transfer
with another word size fails with -ENOPROTOOPT ("you can't yet change
bits_per_word in transfers").

The MIPI DBI panel drivers (e.g. ili9341 of the Acme Systems XTERM-01
display) send commands in 8 bit words and the pixels in 16 bit words
when the controller supports them, so no frame reaches the display:

  ili9341 spi0.0: SPI transfer failed: -92

The rest of the driver already handles the word size of each transfer:
when it differs, update the BITS field of the chip select register
instead of failing.

Upstream: not sent
Signed-off-by: Angelo Compagnucci <angelo.compagnucci@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-atmel.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-atmel.c b/drivers/spi/spi-atmel.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-atmel.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-atmel.c
@@ -1394,9 +1394,18 @@ static int atmel_spi_one_transfer(struct spi_controller *host,
 	asd = spi->controller_state;
 	bits = (asd->csr >> 4) & 0xf;
 	if (bits != xfer->bits_per_word - 8) {
-		dev_dbg(&spi->dev,
-			"you can't yet change bits_per_word in transfers\n");
-		return -ENOPROTOOPT;
+		int chip_select;
+
+		if (spi_get_csgpiod(spi, 0))
+			chip_select = as->native_cs_for_gpio;
+		else
+			chip_select = spi_get_chipselect(spi, 0);
+
+		/* The chip select is active: only the word size changes */
+		asd->csr = SPI_BFINS(BITS, xfer->bits_per_word - 8, asd->csr);
+		spi_writel(as, CSR0 + 4 * chip_select, asd->csr);
+		if (atmel_spi_is_v2(as))
+			spi_writel(as, CSR0, asd->csr);
 	}
 
 	/*
